---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';
import { seoServicesHreflangs } from '../data/internationalSeoPages.js';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How much do SEO services cost in the UK?',
    answer: 'Independent UK pricing guides typically put local and small-business SEO at £300 to £1,500 a month, mainstream agency retainers at £1,100 to £3,600, and enterprise campaigns at £5,000 to £25,000 or more — with London agencies charging a 20 to 40 per cent premium over regional firms. We scope every campaign individually and agree a fixed monthly figure in GBP before work starts, so there are no conversion surprises. Because you are not funding a London office, more of that figure buys actual SEO work.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does SEO take to work in the UK market?',
    answer: 'Expect months one and two to be groundwork — audit, technical fixes, content foundations — with little visible movement. Competitive UK terms usually show meaningful gains between months four and six, then compound. Faster is possible: Speediance UK grew organic traffic 119% within three months. But any agency promising fixed results by a fixed date is guessing, and we would rather set expectations we can beat.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you guarantee page 1 rankings on Google?',
    answer: 'No — and you should walk away from anyone who says yes. Google itself warns against guaranteed-ranking claims because nobody controls the algorithm. What we can show is a published, numbers-included track record for UK-market clients and a method we will explain before you pay anything. Several of our case studies state outright that we do not guarantee identical results. That honesty is deliberate.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What does a monthly SEO retainer actually include?',
    answer: 'A typical month covers technical monitoring and fixes, on-page optimisation, British English content production or briefs, UK-relevant link outreach, and a plain-English report showing rankings, traffic, work completed and next steps. The mix shifts with your campaign phase — month one is audit-heavy, later months lean into content and authority. You keep full access to your Google Analytics and Search Console data throughout.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Why would a UK business use an SEO agency in the Philippines?',
    answer: 'Senior delivery at sensible prices. Typical UK retainers run £1,100 to £3,600 a month, a chunk of which funds offices, sales teams and account layers. We deliver the same strategy, technical work, content direction and reporting from the Philippines, so more of your budget goes into the work itself. UK clients such as UK Auction List have publicly reviewed us after more than 18 months of partnership — the model holds up.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do the time zones work between the UK and the Philippines?',
    answer: 'The Philippines is 7 to 8 hours ahead of the UK. Our afternoon overlaps your morning, so calls sit comfortably at 9:00 or 10:00 UK time, and work we complete during our day is waiting in your inbox before you start yours. Most clients find the overnight rhythm faster than same-timezone agencies that batch work weekly.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Will my content be written in British English?',
    answer: 'Yes. Content for UK campaigns is written and edited in British English — optimisation not optimization, colour not color — with UK terminology, prices in pounds and buyer language that reads naturally to a UK audience. AI-assisted drafts always pass through human editorial review before anything is delivered.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you build links from UK websites?',
    answer: 'Yes. Link relevance matters for country-level rankings, so UK campaigns prioritise UK-relevant opportunities: publications, industry directories, supplier and partner sites, and digital PR angles that make sense to a British audience. We do not sell bulk link packages, and we will show you where every link comes from.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you tie clients into long contracts?',
    answer: 'Engagement length is agreed in your proposal, and we do not rely on tie-ins to keep clients. Our retention is public: UK Auction List reviewed us after more than 18 months of work, and another client describes roughly three years of continuous partnership. SEO does need time — plan for at least six months to judge it fairly — but you should stay because the numbers justify it, not because a contract says so.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you measure and report SEO results?',
    answer: 'Every campaign runs on your own Google Analytics 4 and Google Search Console accounts, plus SE Ranking for rank and AI-visibility tracking — the same stack behind our published case studies. You get a monthly report in plain English covering rankings, traffic, conversions where tracked, work completed and what happens next. If we vanished tomorrow, all data and access would stay with you.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does SEO still work now that people use ChatGPT and AI Overviews?',
    answer: 'Yes — and it is measurable. Over six months we grew a UK-market sports SaaS client’s AI referral sessions 405% to 4,549, and took a UK self-storage provider from 8 to 61 AI referral sessions converting at 8.2%. Traditional SEO foundations still power AI visibility: crawlable sites, clear entities and citable content are exactly what ChatGPT and Google’s AI Overviews draw on.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I hire a UK agency, a freelancer or an offshore team?',
    answer: 'UK freelancers typically charge £40 to £100 an hour and agency consultants £100 to £250. A good freelancer suits a small scope; an agency adds breadth but also overhead. The honest question is always who does the work and what evidence they publish. Judge us the same way: a named team, published UK case studies with numbers attached, and reviews you can verify on Google.'
  }
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="SEO Services UK | Trusted UK SEO Agency | Bright Forge"
  description="SEO services for UK businesses with published results — +119% organic traffic in 3 months. Senior technical SEO, content and links, minus London prices."
  canonical="https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-uk/"
  type="service"
  faqs={faqs}
  hreflangs={seoServicesHreflangs}
  geoRegion="GB"
  geoPlacename="United Kingdom"
  contentLanguage="en-GB"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        {
          '@type': 'ListItem',
          position: 1,
          name: 'Home',
          item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/'
        },
        {
          '@type': 'ListItem',
          position: 2,
          name: 'SEO Services UK',
          item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-uk/'
        }
      ]
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'Service',
      name: 'SEO Services UK',
      serviceType: 'Search engine optimisation',
      url: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-uk/',
      areaServed: {
        '@type': 'Country',
        name: 'United Kingdom'
      },
      availableLanguage: 'en-GB',
      provider: {
        '@type': 'Organization',
        name: 'Bright Forge SEO',
        url: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/'
      },
      description: 'Search engine optimisation services for UK businesses: technical SEO, British English content, UK-relevant link building, AI search optimisation and transparent monthly reporting.'
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />

  <Hero
    badgeIcon="fas fa-globe-europe"
    badgeText="SEO for UK Businesses"
    title="SEO Services for UK Businesses That Want <span>Proven Results, Not London Retainer Prices</span>"
    breadcrumbCurrent="SEO Services UK"
  >
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>We help UK ecommerce brands, SaaS products and service businesses win visibility on google.co.uk — senior technical SEO, British English content, UK-relevant links and reporting you can verify in your own analytics.</p>
      <p>Bright Forge is based in the Philippines, and we put that on the front page for a reason. You get the deliverables of a good UK SEO company without funding a London office, and every claim on this page links to a published case study.</p>
      <p>Like Speediance UK: organic traffic up 119% in three months. Or UK Auction List, who publicly reviewed us after more than 18 months of partnership.</p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Get a UK SEO Proposal" />
      <ButtonSecondary href="#uk-results" text="See UK Client Results" />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div class="market-visual" aria-label="UK SEO campaign snapshot">
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Your market</span>
          <strong>google.co.uk, AI search, UK buyers and competitors</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node forge">
          <span>Your SEO team</span>
          <strong>Named senior specialists in the Philippines</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Your advantage</span>
          <strong>Work done overnight, ready each UK morning</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="UK SEO proof points">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div><strong>+119% organic traffic</strong><span>Speediance UK, in 3 months</span></div>
        <div><strong>5.0 on Google</strong><span>12 five-star client reviews</span></div>
        <div><strong>18+ month UK partnerships</strong><span>Publicly reviewed by UK Auction List</span></div>
        <div><strong>GBP pricing available</strong><span>Calls in your morning, our afternoon</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="why-us">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why UK businesses choose us</p>
        <h2>The work of a UK SEO agency, <span>without the UK agency overhead</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">A good London SEO company and Bright Forge do the same work: audits, technical fixes, content strategy, links, reporting. The difference is what a pound buys.</p>
        <p>UK retainers carry offices, sales teams and account layers. Ours carry senior SEO time. That is the honest trade — and it is why UK businesses have stayed with us for years rather than months. No mystery outsourcing either: UK agencies quietly subcontract work like ours every day. We are simply the team that says so.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid small">
        <article class="card"><h3>Ecommerce brands</h3><p>Category and product page SEO, technical health and content that captures UK buying intent.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>SaaS &amp; B2B</h3><p>Feature, comparison and use-case pages plus authority building for competitive UK software terms.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Service businesses</h3><p>Service and location page strategy for firms that win work through enquiries, not footfall.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>UK agencies</h3><p>Fulfilment under your brand via our <a href="/white-label-seo-services-philippines/">white label SEO services</a>.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="uk-results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">UK client results</p>
        <h2>UK SEO results <span>with the numbers attached</span></h2>
        <p>Every figure below comes from a published case study, measured in Google Analytics 4, Google Search Console and SE Ranking — not stock claims.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Fitness Ecommerce</p>
          <p class="result-metric">+119%</p>
          <h3>Speediance UK — organic traffic in 3 months</h3>
          <p>Clicks grew from 2.16K to 4.74K and impressions rose 135% for a smart home gym brand competing in the crowded UK fitness equipment market.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/speediance-uk-fitness-seo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Sports SaaS · AI Search</p>
          <p class="result-metric">+405%</p>
          <h3>Football team management SaaS — AI referral sessions</h3>
          <p>4,549 sessions from AI platforms in six months, 92.3% via ChatGPT, with 239 AI link citations tracked across five platforms.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-sports-saas-geo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Self-Storage · AI Search</p>
          <p class="result-metric">+662%</p>
          <h3>UK self-storage provider — LLM referrals</h3>
          <p>AI referral sessions grew from 8 to 61 in six months and converted at 8.2% — with ChatGPT driving every tracked conversion.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-self-storage-geo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Bridal Ecommerce · AI Search</p>
          <p class="result-metric">+1,660%</p>
          <h3>Bridal retailer — AI referral sessions</h3>
          <p>AI referrals rose from 5 to 88 sessions at a 70.5% engagement rate, built on 71.6% higher search visibility and 8,600 ranking keywords.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-bridal-ecommerce-geo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="quote-grid">
        <figure class="quote-card">
          <blockquote>“Bright Forge SEO delivered exceptional results for our fitness equipment brand... The consistent uptick in engagement has reinforced our brand credibility in the competitive fitness market.”</blockquote>
          <figcaption>Luke, Marketing Director, Speediance UK</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote-card">
          <blockquote>“We've been working with Ben and Bright Forge SEO for over 18 months, with the primary focus being our SEO needs. They deliver excellent results.”</blockquote>
          <figcaption>UK Auction List, property auctions platform</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote-card">
          <blockquote>“Working with Bright Forge SEO has been a huge benefit for TeamStats. They understand our needs and deliver consistently.”</blockquote>
          <figcaption>Tom Stanbury, TeamStats (UK)</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="services">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we deliver</p>
        <h2>Full-service search engine optimisation <span>for the UK market</span></h2>
        <p>Our SEO services cover the full stack — technical, on-page, content, authority and AI search — run as one campaign against your real UK competitors, not a fixed task list.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-grid">
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-search"></i><h3>SEO audits</h3><p>Technical, content and authority diagnosis with prioritised fixes — the map before the journey.</p><a class="card-link" href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-sitemap"></i><h3>Technical SEO</h3><p>Crawlability, indexation, site speed, schema and structure — the foundations UK rankings sit on.</p><a class="card-link" href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">Technical SEO services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i><h3>On-page SEO</h3><p>Titles, headings, internal links and page structure tuned to how UK buyers actually search.</p><a class="card-link" href="/on-page-seo-services-philippines/">On-page SEO services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-pen-nib"></i><h3>Content SEO</h3><p>British English content mapped to UK search demand, buyer language and commercial intent.</p><a class="card-link" href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">Content SEO services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-key"></i><h3>Keyword research</h3><p>UK demand mapped to pages, including the spelling, phrasing and intent differences that matter.</p><a class="card-link" href="/keyword-research-services/">Keyword research →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-link"></i><h3>Link building &amp; digital PR</h3><p>Relevance-led links from UK publications, directories and industry sites. No spam packages, ever.</p><a class="card-link" href="/backlink-seo-services-philippines/">Link building services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i><h3>AI Search Optimization</h3><p>Entity clarity, citations and answer-ready structure so UK buyers find you in ChatGPT and AI Overviews.</p><a class="card-link" href="/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/">AI search services →</a></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-map-marker-alt"></i><h3>Local SEO</h3><p>Local visibility for UK businesses that win customers city by city, suburb by suburb.</p><a class="card-link" href="/local-seo-services-philippines/">Local SEO services →</a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="grid-note">Replatforming or redesigning? Our <a href="/website-migration-services/">website migration services</a> protect hard-won UK rankings through the switch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="campaign">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Month by month</p>
        <h2>What a UK SEO campaign <span>actually looks like</span></h2>
        <p>Most agencies keep timelines vague because honesty scares off leads. Here is the real shape of a typical campaign — including the part where early months produce groundwork, not enquiries.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="phase-grid">
        <article class="phase-card">
          <p class="phase-step">Month 1</p>
          <h3>Diagnose</h3>
          <p>Full technical, content and authority audit against your UK competitors. GA4 and Search Console access in week one, keyword research, and a prioritised roadmap you could take anywhere.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="phase-card">
          <p class="phase-step">Months 2–3</p>
          <h3>Fix &amp; build</h3>
          <p>Technical fixes shipped, on-page optimisation live, first British English content published, link outreach underway. Honestly: expect foundations here, not leads.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="phase-card">
          <p class="phase-step">Months 4–6</p>
          <h3>Momentum</h3>
          <p>Rankings move on tracked commercial terms and organic traffic trends upward. This is where competitive UK campaigns typically show their first meaningful gains.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="phase-card">
          <p class="phase-step">Months 7–12</p>
          <h3>Compound</h3>
          <p>Authority matures, keyword coverage widens, gains get defended through algorithm updates, and strategy is re-tested quarterly against results.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="grid-note">Every month closes with a plain-English report, and you can watch progress between reports in our <a href="/seo-command-centre/">SEO Command Centre</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing, honestly</p>
        <h2>How much do SEO services <span>cost in the UK?</span></h2>
        <p>UK pricing guides consistently put agency SEO between £500 and £20,000+ a month depending on scope. Almost no agency publishes this on its services page. Here is the market, in the open.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="price-table">
        <div class="price-row price-head">
          <span>Campaign type</span><span>Typical UK market rate</span><span>What that usually buys</span>
        </div>
        <div class="price-row">
          <span>Local &amp; small business SEO</span><span>£300–£1,500/month</span><span>Local campaigns from around £300–£500; guides warn budgets under £500–£1,000 usually buy templated, automated work.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="price-row">
          <span>SME / national campaigns</span><span>£1,100–£3,600/month</span><span>The most-cited “typical agency” band; meaningful national campaigns generally start around £1,500.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="price-row">
          <span>B2B &amp; mid-market</span><span>£1,500–£5,000/month</span><span>Competitive niches, larger sites, content and digital PR at volume.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="price-row">
          <span>Enterprise</span><span>£5,000–£25,000+/month</span><span>Multi-market, multi-team programmes. One-off audits typically run £500–£5,000 across the market.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="two-col pricing-cols">
        <div>
          <h3>What changes the price</h3>
          <ul class="tick-list">
            <li>How competitive your niche is on google.co.uk</li>
            <li>Site size and accumulated technical debt</li>
            <li>Content volume needed to close the gap</li>
            <li>Your authority deficit versus ranking competitors</li>
            <li>Local, national or international scope</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Where the offshore model changes the maths</h3>
          <p>London agencies typically charge a 20–40% premium over regional firms — and part of every UK retainer funds rent, sales and account management rather than delivery. Our overheads are Philippine, our output is senior, and we quote a fixed GBP monthly figure after seeing your site. One warning: cheap SEO is cheap everywhere. If an offshore quote looks too good to be true, it is templated work with a discount label on it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="choose">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Buyer's guide</p>
        <h2>How to choose an SEO agency <span>in the UK</span></h2>
        <p>Whether you shortlist a London SEO company, a freelance consultant or us, the same six checks separate real operators from invoice factories.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="choose-grid">
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">1</span><h3>Demand named humans</h3><p>Ask who actually does the work — employees, freelancers, or an outsourced team the agency never mentions. We are that outsourced team; we just say so, with names.</p></article>
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">2</span><h3>Ask for numbers, not adjectives</h3><p>“Great results” is marketing. A baseline, a result, a timeframe and a measurement method is evidence. Our case studies publish all four.</p></article>
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">3</span><h3>Keep your own accounts</h3><p>GA4, Search Console and your website should live in your name. Walk away from any provider that insists on owning your data or access.</p></article>
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">4</span><h3>Interrogate the links</h3><p>Ask where links come from and request samples. If the answer is vague, you are buying a link network that a Google update will eventually torch.</p></article>
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">5</span><h3>Treat guarantees as red flags</h3><p>Guaranteed page-one rankings is the oldest trick in this industry. Nobody controls Google — agencies that promise it are selling certainty they do not have.</p></article>
        <article class="choose-card"><span class="choose-num">6</span><h3>Read the exit terms</h3><p>Long tie-ins protect weak agencies. Check what happens when you leave — you should keep every page, link and account the campaign built.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="grid-note">Apply that checklist to everyone on your shortlist, including us. This page was built to pass it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="ai-search">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">AI search &amp; GEO</p>
        <h2>Your UK buyers now ask <span>ChatGPT before they ask Google</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">AI Overviews sit on top of google.co.uk results, and ChatGPT recommends specific brands to UK buyers every day. We are one of the few agencies measuring this properly — with five published AI-search case studies, all tracked from August 2025 to January 2026 in GA4, Search Console and SE Ranking.</p>
        <p>For a fintech SaaS serving the UK market, AI platforms drove 1,322 referral sessions averaging 7 minutes 11 seconds on site, reaching users in 80 countries. That is not a novelty channel — it is qualified demand, and the same foundations that rank you on Google get you cited by AI. <a href="/case-studies/ai-fintech-saas-geo/">See the fintech AI-search case study</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timezone-card">
        <h3>What our AI-search data shows</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>ChatGPT dominates</strong> — 72% to 92% of tracked AI referrals across our case studies come via ChatGPT</li>
          <li><strong>AI visitors engage</strong> — every tracked AI platform averaged over 5 minutes per session for our fintech client</li>
          <li><strong>AI traffic converts</strong> — 8.2% conversion rate on AI referrals for a UK self-storage provider</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="industries">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Sector experience</p>
        <h2>Specialist SEO for <span>your industry</span></h2>
        <p>Generic SEO produces generic results. These are sectors where we run dedicated playbooks — several backed by the UK-market case studies above.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="industry-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/football-soccer-seo-services/">Football &amp; sports</a></h3><p>From grassroots platforms to sports SaaS — including the football team management client whose AI referrals grew 405%.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/home-services-seo/">Home services &amp; trades</a></h3><p>Enquiry-driven SEO for the firms UK homeowners search for first: heating, electrics, roofing, clearance and more.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/real-estate-seo-services/">Property &amp; real estate</a></h3><p>Listings visibility, local landing pages and authority building for agents, portals and property platforms.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/finance-crypto-seo-services/">Finance &amp; fintech</a></h3><p>Compliance-aware SEO for a sector where trust signals decide rankings — informed by our fintech SaaS AI-search work.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/gaming-seo-services/">Gaming</a></h3><p>Search strategies for gaming brands competing in fast-moving, content-hungry UK niches.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/pet-seo-services/">Pets</a></h3><p>Ecommerce and service SEO for one of the UK's most passionate — and most searched — consumer markets.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="grid-note">Our published portfolio also spans fitness equipment, bridal, self-storage, boiler spares, consulting and more — browse <a href="/case-studies/">all case studies</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="team">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who does the work</p>
        <h2>Named SEO specialists, <span>not an anonymous back office</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Most offshore providers hide who does the work. Most UK agencies hide that some of it is outsourced. Here is our answer to both.</p>
